Implement a new feature in perfSonic API Studio: **Upload Payload** (Parse requirement payload text file and auto-populate requests into API Studio).

## Goal

Allow user to upload a text file containing one or more API request definitions in a semi-structured format (developer payload notes), parse it intelligently, and populate new requests into existing API Studio.

⚠ Scope:

* Only parse and populate requests.
* Do NOT execute requests.
* Do NOT trigger certificates, correlation, parameterization, or script generation.
  User will review and run later.

---

## Add UI

Add button in API Studio:

```text id="1分快三1"
Upload Payload
```

Click opens file picker for `.txt` (support plain text first).

---

## Expected input format (flexible/semi-structured)

Input may contain section headings, but key/value pairs always follow pattern:

```text id="2分快三2"
Key: Value
```

Examples user may provide:

```text id="3分快三3"
Request:
Endpoint: https://host/api/v1/payment
Method: POST

Headers:
Accept: */*
Content-Type: application/json
X-Session: {...}

Body:
{
 "clientId":"123"
}

Request:
Endpoint: https://host/api/v1/report
Method: GET

Headers:
Accept: */*
```

Possible synonyms to support:

* Endpoint:
* URL:
* Request:
* Method:
* Headers:
* Header:
* Body:
* Payload:

Parser should be tolerant to minor formatting variations.

---

## Parsing requirements

Build intelligent parser to:

### Detect request boundaries

Start a new request when:

* "Request:" appears
* OR new Endpoint/URL encountered after prior request complete

Support multiple requests in one file.

---

## Extract:

Per request capture:

* URL
* Method
* Headers (key:value pairs under Headers section)
* Body (raw multi-line content under Body/Payload section)
* If no Body for GET, keep null

---

## Smart body handling

Body may span multiple lines.

Parser should preserve raw body until next recognized section or next request boundary.

Do not corrupt JSON formatting.

---

## Request naming

Auto-generate request names:

```text id="4分快三4"
Request1_HHMMSS
Request2_HHMMSS
```

Use timestamp/random suffix so names are unique.

No two generated requests should collide.

---

## Populate behavior

Important:
If user already has existing requests in API Studio:

* Do NOT overwrite existing requests
* Do NOT clear existing requests

Use existing **+ New Request** functionality programmatically.

Append parsed requests one after another as newly added requests.

Reuse existing request model and request creation logic.

---

## Mapping into API Studio

Populate parsed values into same fields a manually created request uses:

* method dropdown
* URL field
* header section
* body editor

Requests should appear in UI exactly as if user created them manually.

---

## Validation

If parser finds:

* no valid requests
* missing URL in request block

show actionable error.

Example:

```text id="5分快三5"
No valid requests found in uploaded payload.
Ensure payload uses Key: Value format (Endpoint:, Method:, Headers:, Body:).
```

---

## Important parser behavior

Prefer resilient parsing over rigid parsing.

If unknown sections appear, ignore them unless they help parsing.

Focus on extracting usable requests, not perfect document interpretation.

---

## Architecture

Implement parser as reusable backend module (not UI-only parsing), so same parser can later be extended for:

* Confluence ingestion
* JIRA ingestion

Design with future source adapters in mind.

---

## Deliverable

User flow:

1. Click Upload Payload
2. Upload text file
3. Parser extracts requests
4. Requests auto-added into API Studio via +New Request logic
5. User reviews, adds certificate if needed, and runs manually

No execution in this feature.
